------------------------------------------------------------------------
Heritage
------------------------------------------------------------------------
C⏚ ("C-Ground") is the continuation of the Synflow Cx toolchain, originally
developed by Synflow (until 2021) and maintained and evolved by Neosyn since
2024. Portions of this codebase originate from that work.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope
------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repository contains the C⏚ language frontend and the Verilog code
generator only. The fast (bytecode) simulator, the VHDL backend, the license/
activation tooling, and the production IP cores are part of the commercial
Neosyn distribution and are not included here. See https://neosyn.io/open.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Standard library
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The standard-library Verilog under
fragments/com.neosyn.ide.libraries/lib/verilog/src (FIFOs, RAMs,
synchronizers, DDR mux/demux, Divide, Multiply) and its C⏚ declarations
(the .cg files in plugins/com.neosyn.cg/model) are (c) Neosyn and are not
covered by the Mozilla Public License. They are free to use, including
commercially, as part of hardware designs generated by the C⏚ compiler,
whether this open-source compiler or the commercial distribution. They may
not be extracted for use on their own, reverse-engineered, or redistributed
except as part of such a design or of the C⏚ compiler. Each file's header
states these terms. The Verilog is provided in a non-readable form that keeps
every module's name, parameters and ports.

